  "rationale": "Moves the Windows, Linux, iOS, Android and web UI host sources, their headers and their platform-only tests from core/ into integrations/legacy-platform-hosts/ unchanged apart from include paths and comments. The Android render shell and Choreographer pacer are among them. Every platform builds the same sources under the same conditions: the package attaches them to the core/view targets, and pulp-jni, PulpAndroid.cmake and PulpWebUi.cmake name the new paths. No renderer, design-import, Chromium or packaging behaviour changes, the installed SDK keeps the same headers and sources at the same destinations, and no authority moves.",
